.\" Manual page for git-reviewer. git opens this for `git reviewer --help`,
.\" because it reads --help on any subcommand as a request for its man page.
.TH GIT-REVIEWER 1 "2026-09-25" "git-reviewer" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
git-reviewer, reviewer \- review local git changes in your browser, and hand the review to a coding agent
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git reviewer
.RI [ repository ]
.RB [ \-p
.IR port ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-open ]
.br
.B git reviewer export
.RI [ repository ]
.RB [ \-\-format
.IR json | prompt ]
.RB [ \-\-file
.IR path ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Opens the uncommitted changes of a git repository, or its last commit on a
clean tree, as a pull-request style review in your browser: inline comments
on any line, threaded follow-ups, and comparisons between branches, tags and
commits \(em reviewed together, one at a time, or as a run.
.PP
With something reading its output, it writes the finished review there the
moment you submit it, and exits:
.PP
.RS
.B git reviewer | claude \-p "Apply this review."
.RE
.PP
On a terminal it says where the review was saved and keeps serving until
the tab is closed.
.PP
The package is installed as
.BR git\-reviewer ,
which git runs as
.BR "git reviewer" .
.B reviewer
is the same program under a shorter name.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B export
Print the saved review of a repository to stdout, as JSON or as a prompt for
a coding agent.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port " \fIn\fR"
Port to listen on. The default is 4500; if it is taken, a free one is used.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-open
Print the address instead of opening a browser.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-format " \fIjson\fR|\fIprompt\fR"
Export format. The default is json.
.TP
.BI \-\-file " path"
Export only the comments on one repository-relative file.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage. Under git, use
.BR \-h :
git takes
.B \-\-help
to mean this page.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B git reviewer
Review the repository you are standing in.
.TP
.B git reviewer | claude \-p """Apply this review."""
Review it, then hand it straight to an agent.
.TP
.B git reviewer export . \-\-format prompt | claude \-p """Apply this review."""
Hand over a review written earlier.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/dheerajjha/reviewer
